-- Measures known-size construction followed by a known-size transform.
use sequence as items.
use testing as check.

function double(value unsigned) giving unsigned {
  give value multiply 2.
}

dynamic values is items.sized[unsigned](10`000) try.
dynamic index of type unsigned is 0.
while index less than 10`000 {
  set values at index to index.
  increase index by 1.
}

constant doubled is items.map[unsigned, unsigned](values, double) try.
after {
  items.release[unsigned](values) fallback nothing.
  items.release[unsigned](doubled) fallback nothing.
}

check.number(items.length[unsigned](doubled), 10`000).
check.number(doubled at 9`999, 19`998).
